{"segs": ["PA_ja_89:0.2", "PA_ja_89:0.3"], "en": "The First Collection (Ekakanipāta), Chapter on the Non-Drinker (Apāyimhavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_89:0.4"], "en": "9. The Kuhaka Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_89:1.1", "PA_ja_89:1.2"], "en": "“Indeed, your words were gentle, as you spoke with friendliness;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_89:1.3"], "en": "\"You were attached to a mere blade of grass,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_89:1.4"], "en": "yet you did not carry off a hundred coins.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_89:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the Ninth Jātaka, the Kuhaka-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
